<title>AUSTRALIA: RUGBY UNION-AUSTRALIAN BARBARIANS BEAT FRANCE 26-25.</title>
<headline>RUGBY UNION-AUSTRALIAN BARBARIANS BEAT FRANCE 26-25.</headline>
<dateline>NEWCASTLE, Australia 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian Barbarians beat France 26-25 (halftime 12-12) in a rugby union tour match on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Australian Barbarians - Try: Mitch Hardy. Penalties: Christian Warner (6), Manuel Edmonds.</p>
<p>France - Tries: David Dantiacq, Didier Casadei, Christophe Lamaison. Conversion: Sebastien Viars, Richard Dourthe. Penalties: Viars, Dourthe.</p>
